parrot-janitor (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Processes tab: live CPU/RAM table with sustained-runaway detection
    (configurable CPU and duration thresholds), binary path + owning Debian
    package identification, plain-English process descriptions, filter and
    multi-select kill with confirmation and optional polkit escalation.
  * Resources tab: per-thread utilisation bars with heat colouring, rolling
    7-minute CPU/RAM history chart, load average, memory split into
    in-use / reclaimable cache / free, swap, and thermal-zone temperatures.
  * Ports tab: every listening socket from ss classified by scope, then
    verified with a real TLS handshake or protocol banner read; explicit
    open/closed connect-test of 36 well-known ports; read-only ufw/nft
    firewall view through polkit.
  * Docker tab: container list with live CPU/memory and bulk start/stop/
    restart.
  * Snapshots tab: create, inspect and delete read-only btrfs snapshots of @
    and @home under /.snapshots, all authenticated through pkexec.
  * Disk tab: size overview, big-file finder, empty trash, purge pip cache
    and delete a selected cache entry, each behind a confirmation.
  * Custom icon and desktop launcher.
  * Headless self-test via `parrot-janitor --smoke`.

